it_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":28251,"output_tokens":913,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"d4185dda7733d3d8075b4850b6d4ac7bd0f9044b4f3af80637e58988bd31eaac"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":24887,"output_tokens":1651,"requests":3}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State whether ${...} placeholders are permitted in header names, and if so that name validation (denied set + token chars) runs on the resolved name after substitution (mirroring the value ordering); otherwise state names are validated as literals with placeholders disallowed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.265,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The ordering rationale is framed entirely around values: 'a configured ${env:GATEWAY_TAG} where GATEWAY_TAG is foo\\r\\nInjected: bar passes a check applied to the literal'","Name validation is described as 'header names in the denied set ... names outside RFC 7230 token characters' with no statement about whether names undergo ${...} substitution","ABSENCE: no disposition for a placeholder in a header name (e.g. ${env:HDR_NAME}: value), so an implementer cannot tell if a name is validated as a literal or after substitution"],"finding":"The substitute-first-then-validate ordering and denied-set/token/control-char checks are specified for header VALUES, but the plan never states whether ${env:...}/${run:...} placeholders may appear in header NAMES, nor whether name validation (denied set, RFC 7230 token chars) runs before or after any name-side substitution — leaving the name-side data flow underspecified where it feeds the security-critical denied-set check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc60dc178fac9c4a0","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Ordering: substitute first, then validate' and the denied-set paragraph","norm_id":"nceba14411a6ee2f8","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator configures a header whose NAME is ${env:SOMEVAR}; if names are substituted but validated before substitution, a resolved name could bypass the denied-set/token check the same way the value case would"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the no-vendor-header-name-hardcoding portability guarantee in the Approach section so the scan AC maps to described work.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7237,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Approach argues 'A denylist rather than an allowlist because arbitrary gateway header names are the point of the feature' but never states the code must avoid hardcoding vendor-specific header names.","The scanned literals x-litellm-/langfuse_/helicone- are introduced only in the AC line, with no covering description in the body."],"finding":"The portability guarantee proven by AC 'No gateway-vendor header name appears as a string constant in shipped code' targets vendor literals (x-litellm-, langfuse_, helicone-) that never appear as a described requirement in the Approach section; the AC verifies a constraint the plan body does not state.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f29304e4ab6e05037","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'No gateway-vendor header name appears as a string constant'","norm_id":"n0585e4823f26dca2","priority":0.2263,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer reads the Approach and does not realize a portability/no-vendor-hardcoding invariant is a design requirement, then is surprised by the scan test."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to Approach noting that headers.py must not hardcode any vendor-specific header name, which the scan test enforces.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"Reconcile the new headers.py ${env:VAR} grammar/resolution with the existing production resolver (_ENV_RE + sub_env in workflow/executor.py, mirrored in lint_refs.py): either reuse/extract the shared regex and unset-error handling, or state an explicit rationale for a deliberate fork (e.g. keeping the config layer free of a workflow-module dependency, or the divergent validation surface).","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:73 `_ENV_RE = re.compile(r\"\\$\\{env:([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\}\")`","src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:304-308 `def sub_env(...): if var not in os.environ: raise ExpressionError(f\"environment variable {var!r} is not set\")` — same unset-is-hard-error disposition the plan restates for ${env:VAR}","src/rebar/llm/workflow/lint_refs.py:63 defines the identical `_ENV_RE` token in the lint layer","Plan text treats the ${env:...} grammar as self-originating ('the grammar is self-contained') with no reference to the existing resolver — an unreconciled duplicate grammar for the same token"],"finding":"The ${env:VAR} grammar and resolution the plan proposes to build fresh in headers.py already exist in production as _ENV_RE + sub_env in src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py (same syntax, same unset-is-hard-error semantics), mirrored in workflow/lint_refs.py; the plan does not acknowledge or reconcile with it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feea82b91fe843250","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'headers.py owns that set and the ${run:...} key vocabulary'; Scope — 'src/rebar/llm/headers.py (new) — grammar, ${env:...} resolution'","norm_id":"n1d4427e384958e60","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The two ${env:...} grammars drift (e.g. one accepts a var-name char the other rejects), so a header value that lints as valid in a workflow is rejected by headers.py or vice versa","A future change to env-indirection semanti